body:
**Problem**

`BlurhashDisplay` constructs a fresh `Future<ui.Image?>` inside its `build()` method, so every parent rebuild restarts the pixels→`ui.Image` decode and momentarily reverts to the gradient fallback. On a 50+ tile profile grid that gets churned by `BackgroundPublishBloc` upload-progress emissions (#3605), this causes visible flicker across the whole grid and redundant decode work.

**Evidence**

`mobile/lib/widgets/blurhash_display.dart:70`:

```dart
return FutureBuilder<ui.Image?>(
  future: _createImageFromPixels(            // <-- new Future per build()
    _blurhashData!.pixels!,
    _blurhashData!.width,
    _blurhashData!.height,
  ),
  builder: (context, snapshot) {
    if (snapshot.hasData && snapshot.data != null) {
      return CustomPaint(...);
    }
    // Fall back to gradient while image is being created
    return _buildGradientFallback();
  },
);
```

Each `build()` call creates a new `Future` (different identity), so `FutureBuilder` treats it as a fresh request. The builder runs once with `snapshot.hasData == false` (returning the gradient), then again when the new future resolves (returning the painter). The decoded `ui.Image` is computed but not cached across rebuilds.

**Impact**

Medium. Visible only under the parent-rebuild churn caused by #3605 (BackgroundPublishBloc progress ticks during active upload), but on a profile grid with 50+ thumbnails the cost compounds across every visible tile. Each rebuild does a `decodeImageFromPixels` call per visible tile and briefly flashes the gradient fallback before the new `ui.Image` resolves. Reported as part of significant low-end-Android lag in PR #4191 review by @hm21 (https://github.com/divinevideo/divine-mobile/pull/4191#pullrequestreview-4257933582).

**Effort**

Low. Cache the future in `State` so its identity is stable across rebuilds — recompute only when `_blurhashData` actually changes:

```dart
Future<ui.Image?>? _imageFuture;

void _decodeBlurhash() {
  // ... existing logic, then:
  if (mounted && data != null) {
    setState(() {
      _blurhashData = data;
      _imageFuture = _createImageFromPixels(
        data.pixels!,
        data.width,
        data.height,
      );
    });
  }
}

@override
Widget build(BuildContext context) {
  if (_blurhashData?.pixels != null && _imageFuture != null) {
    return FutureBuilder<ui.Image?>(
      future: _imageFuture,    // stable across rebuilds
      builder: ...,
    );
  }
  // ... existing fallbacks
}
```

**Related**

- #3605 — `context.watch<BackgroundPublishBloc>()` causes the parent rebuilds that surface this.
- #4190 / PR #4191 — capped `memCacheWidth` on the network image; this is the next layer of the same lag report.

**Source**: PR #4191 review (low-end Android repro from @hm21).
